%N A399001 The binomial matrix of the Fibonacci numbers, square array read by upward antidiagonals.
%C A399001 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A399001 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A399001 A(n, n) = F(n), the Fibonacci numbers.
%F A399001 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * F(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
